		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Requete select avec sortie sous forme de colone]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=11484#p11484"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Juste pour ceux que çà intéresserait :</p><p>ma solution : </p><br /><p>select * from crosstab(<br />&#039;<br />select id1, position, pers from<br />(<br />&#160; &#160; select r2.id1, r2.pers,count(r2.id1) as position <br />&#160; &#160; from <br />&#160; &#160; (<br />&#160; &#160; select t1.id as id1, t2.id as id2,(t2.nom||&#039;&#039; &#039;&#039;||t2.prenom)::varchar(40) as pers from t1 join t2 on t1.id = t2.id_t1<br />&#160; &#160; )r1, <br />&#160; &#160; (<br />&#160; &#160; select t1.id as id1, t2.id as id2,(t2.nom||&#039;&#039; &#039;&#039;||t2.prenom)::varchar(40) as pers from t1 join t2 on t1.id = t2.id_t1<br />&#160; &#160; )r2 <br />&#160; &#160; where r1.id2 &lt;= r2.id2 and r1.id1 = r2.id1<br />&#160; &#160; group by r2.id1, r2.id2, r2.pers<br />&#160; &#160; order by r2.id1, r2.id2<br />)out1 where position &lt;=3 &#039; )<br />AS ct(row_name integer, category_1 varchar(40), category_2 varchar(40), category_3 varchar(40))</p><br /><p>je ne sais pas s&#039;il y a plus simple mais la ca tourne......</p><br /><p>merci encore à Marc</p>]]></content>
